=== Crop Growth ===
{{Main|Crop Growth}}
The {{stat|Crop Growth}} influences how fast crops planted in the Garden grow. Every {{stat|Crop Growth|+1}} increases the growing speed by {{green|+1%}}, up to a maximum of {{stat|Crop Growth|210}} at {{Garden|15}}, {{Attr|Crop Speed|X}} Attribute ({{item|Locust Shard}}) and [[DNA Analysis Milestone]] {{romnum|6}}. As for plants growing in the [[Greenhouse]], the conversion is reduced to {{green|+0.25%}} growing speed per {{stat|Crop Growth|+1}}.

Crops in '''The Garden''' do not require light to grow at maximum speed, but they do require water. Crops will not grow at all on completely dry soil (even with {{item|Bone Meal}} or {{item|Enchanted Bone Meal}}), and will receive a {{red|-40%}} growth speed debuff on soil that is not fully moist.

{{item|Pumpkin}} and {{item|Melon Slice|alt=Melon}} plants only require water for the stem to grow. After it is grown, {{item|Pumpkin}}s and {{item|Melon}} will sprout regardless of soil moisture.

==== Crop Growing Mechanics ====
Every 10 game ticks (0.5s) the server sends a number of random ticks to randomly selected crop blocks within a plot. If a crop receives a random tick, it grows by one growth stage. If a crop is already fully grown, nothing happens. Due to this behavior, harvested crops replenish fastest when no crops are yet fully grown, and slowest when almost all crops are already grown.

Crops only grow if the player is in the Garden, regardless of distance to the plot. They do not grow if the player is outside the Garden or offline.

=== Pests ===
{{Main|Pest}}

After reaching {{Garden|5}}, [[Garden Pest]]s will have a chance of appearing whenever a [[Player]] breaks a crop in {{zone|The Garden}}. There are {{Green|13}} types of pests that can spawn. When {{Green|4}} or more pests are on '''The Garden''', a [[Player]]'s {{statname|farming fortune}} will decrease up to {{Green|8}} pests. {{statname|farming fortune}} can be restored by capturing the pests, or can be avoided by having more {{Stat|Bonus Pest Chance}}. Pests can also be exchanged at {{NPCSprite|Pesthunter Phillip}} for temporary {{statname|farming fortune}}.

=== The Desk ===
The '''Desk''' is a key feature of {{zone|The Garden}}, which can be found at the barn plot. It allows the [[player]] to configure [[#Plots|Plots]], add [[#Crop Upgrades|Crop Upgrades]], access [[#SkyMart|SkyMart]], view [[#Garden Milestones|Crop Milestones]], and view and change the [[#Barn Skins|Barn's Skin]]. It can also be opened using the <code>/desk</code> [[command]] (only works while in {{zone|The Garden}}).

{{:The Desk/UI}}

The cost of your garden plots that ''you'' may have will likely be different than the ones shown above in the UI. This is because the costs shown in the above UI are if the plots are bought in numerical order. The cost of a plot depends on '''the "tier" of the plot and how many plots you have already unlocked in that "tier"''', not the plot number. The "tier" of a specific plot is determined by its {{Skl|Garden}} Level requirement, which can either be 1, 3, 5, or 7. In addition, the cost(s) for all remaining plot(s) that have not been unlocked in a specific tier will all be the same, unlike the UI above, where the plot costs are all different. This means that if ''n'' plots have been bought in a single tier, the cost for every other plot in the tier will be cost of the ''nth'' plot of the tier, shown above in the UI.

For example, if Plots 1, 2, and 3 were bought, Plot 4 will cost {{Green|Compost}} {{DarkGray|x8}}. But if Plots 1 and 3 were only bought, the costs for ''both'' Plots 2 and 4 will be {{Green|Compost}} {{DarkGray|x4}}, as that is the cost in the UI for Plot 3, after two "Tier 1" plots have already been bought. The costs for plots in other tiers will remain unaffected, as they are only affected by other plots in their "tier".

=== Composter ===
{{Main|Composter}}
The '''Composter''' is a feature that allows the player to turn crops and other [[Organic Matter]] into [[Compost]]. It requires [[Machine Fuel]] such as {{Item|Biofuel}} to operate. It can create 1 Compost every 10 minutes, with each Compost requiring {{Green|4000}} Organic Matter and {{Stat|Fuel|2000}}.

=== Plots ===
The Garden has 24 '''Plots''' in a {{Green|5x5}} grid, with the Barn in the middle. Each plot is {{Green|96x96}} blocks. To unlock a plot, the player has to spend {{Item|Compost}} or {{Item|Compost Bundle}}s at the [[#The Desk|Desk]]. There is also a {{skl|Garden|Level}} requirement. After unlocking the plot, it needs to be cleaned. {{Item|Plot Eraser}} can clean the plot instantly. {{Item|Sam's Scythe}} or a {{Item|Garden Scythe}} can be used to break plants faster. Leaves will decay once the plot is over {{Yellow|70%}} clean. Breaking the following blocks on the plot counts towards cleaning progress:
*{{Item|Dirt}} and {{Item|Grass Block}}s above ground level
*{{Item|Stone}}
*{{Item|Flowers}}
*{{Item|Long Grass}}
*{{Item|Double Tallgrass}}
*{{Item|Wood}}
*{{Item|Leaves}}

After cleaning the plot, the player can paste a preset onto it at the [[#The Desk|Desk]], which will overwrite the blocks on the plot. The player can use default presets for crops, which use the specific crop's corresponding "seed" item. The seeds can be obtained through the [[Bazaar]] if the player has a [[Booster Cookie]] active, or from the player's inventory and [[Sacks]]. The player can also save plots as custom presets, which will only paste non-crop blocks and will not drop blocks broken by the player.

{{Item|Melon Slice}}s and {{Item|Pumpkin}} blocks in the player's inventory will be automatically converted to seeds. Enchanted forms of crops can also be used to paste plots, and the difference will be refunded into the player's inventory once pasting is done. (Note: While this is supposed to work with sacks too, it currently only works with crops in the player's inventory.)

