=== Barn Skins ===
{{Main|Barn Skins}}
'''Barn Skins''' are a type of cosmetic that changes the look of the Barn. They can be applied to the Barn at the [[#The Desk|Desk]].
{{:Barn Skins/UI}}

=== Greenhouse ===
{{Main|Greenhouse}}
After reaching {{Skill|Garden|7}}, the {{NPCSprite|Carpenter}} can visit '''The Garden'''. Completing their offer for the first time grants the {{Item|Greenhouse Blueprint}}, which can be given to {{NPCSprite|Sam}} to unlock the [[Greenhouse]]. 

The [[Greenhouse]] allows the player to plant regular crops and grow [[Mutations]]. Up to {{Green|3}} [[Greenhouse]] plots can be unlocked and placed.

== Bugs ==
*During the tutorial quest, the first visitor currently does not appear. Leaving the Garden (and making sure no one else is on it) and then rejoining it about 10 seconds later should make them appear.

== Trivia ==
<!--*If you are on a [[Stranded]] profile, talking to Tia the Fairy will result in this message: {{Rmt|&fIt's a shame you can't visit public islands. If you ever do, I have a quest for you.}}-->
*The only {{Special}} '''Visitor''' is {{NPCSprite|Spaceman}}. They are not accessible anywhere in [[SkyBlock]].
*The Fear Mongerer '''Visitor''' turns into a bat when leaving the garden.
*Talking to a '''Visitor''' while [[Guesting|being a guest]] on someone else's '''Garden''' will result in the following dialogue. {{Rmt|&fHmm... I haven't seen you around here before. Do you work here?}}.
*Visitors have a variety of lines while waiting in queue, similarly to [[Minions#Minion Dialogue|Minions]].
**One of those lines features one of the visitors asking what is the time, another visitor answers and their dialogue changes with the time. This is the only way to tell SkyBlock time precisely to the minute.
*There is a limit of 64 simultaneous primed [[TNT]] entities on the player's {{Zone|Private Island}} and {{Zone|The Garden}}.
**This limit was added because of {{RN|youtube|SomethingLT}}.<ref>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qH0JOQIUEaw</ref>
*Players do not take any Fall damage on '''Garden'''.
*Just like on {{zone|Private Island}}, dying to the Void doesn't remove {{c}} from the player's purse.
